<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   AgentPro: linphone's decorative "mountains" band - the wave shape across the bottom of every
   assistant screen - drawn as three tinted paths. It is one of their recognisable brand marks,
   so it cannot stay in a white-label product. The same band was removed from the desktop build.

   Made invisible rather than deleted, and the original width/height kept. Nine layouts
   reference this drawable, and several constrain their own views with
   layout_constraintBottom_toTopOf="@id/mountains" - deleting the file breaks the build, and
   removing the ImageView from each layout breaks those chains. Same size, nothing visible, so
   no screen shifts.

   The single path below is required: a <vector> with no path at all fails to inflate at
   runtime (Resources$NotFoundException on this file), which crashed the app on launch. It is
   kept degenerate and fully transparent - fillColor is ignored anyway once android:tint is
   applied by the layouts, so the geometry has to be what makes it invisible, not the colour.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="1084dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="1084"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M0,0L0,0Z" />
</vector>
